   "title": "ICT exports log record-high growth in Oct. amid AI boom",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/economy/20261115/ict-exports-log-record-high-growth-in-oct-amid-ai-boom",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:52:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794732723.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "South Korea's exports of information and communication technology (ICT) products rose at the sharpest pace on record from a year earlier in October, data showed Sunday, driven by the global artificial intelligence (AI) boom. The figure also marked the second-highest monthly total on record, just below the $75.1 billion posted in September.",
   "summary_zh": "数据显示，受全球人工智能（AI）热潮推动，韩国10月信息通信技术（ICT）产品出口额较上年同期创下有记录以来最快增速。这一数字也创下有记录以来第二高的单月总额，仅略低于9月的751亿美元。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "South Korea's exports of information and communication technology (ICT) products rose at the sharpest pace on record from a year earlier in October, data showed Sunday, driven by the global artificial intelligence (AI) boom. Outbound shipments of ICT products came to $70.35 billion in October, more than tripling from $23.29 billion a year earlier, according to data compiled by the Ministry of Science and ICT. The figure also marked the second-highest monthly total on record, just below the $75.1 billion posted in September. The report also showed ICT exports accounted for 61 percent of the country's total outbound shipments of $115.28 billion in October, with the proportion remaining above 60 percent for three consecutive months. Exports of semiconductors shot up 259.4 percent on-year in October to $56.47 billion, driven by strong global demand for premium memory products and persistently high memory prices. Outbound shipments of computers and accessories also reached $5.99 billion in October, growing more than fivefold from a year earlier, led by high-capacity solid-state drives (SSDs) for servers. Exports of mobile phones rose 6.5 percent to $1.71 billion on the back of strong sales of premium models. By destination, exports to China more than tripled to $27.2 billion, driven by gains in semiconductors and computers. Shipments to the United States also grew more than sixfold to $15.56 billion, the report showed",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
