   "summary": "The Philippines, chair of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations for 2026, is hosting the 49th ASEAN Summit and Related Summits from Sunday, November 15, to Tuesday, November 17. During the summit’s closing ceremony, the Philippines will also turn over the ASEAN chairmanship to Singapore, which will lead the bloc in 2027. Check out this page for the latest ASEAN Summit news, photos, videos, and insights.",
   "summary_zh": "菲律宾是2026年东南亚国家联盟轮值主席国，将于11月15日星期日至11月17日星期二主办第49届东盟峰会及相关峰会。在峰会闭幕式上，菲律宾还将把东盟主席国职权移交给新加坡，由新加坡在2027年领导该组织。查看此页面，了解东盟峰会的最新消息、照片、视频和深度解析。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW The global energy crisis, food security, and transnational crime are among the top issues on the table as Southeast Asian leaders and their allies converge in Manila. The Philippines, chair of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations for 2026, is hosting the 49th ASEAN Summit and Related Summits from Sunday, November 15, to Tuesday, November 17. During the summit’s closing ceremony, the Philippines will also turn over the ASEAN chairmanship to Singapore, which will lead the bloc in 2027. Check out this page for the latest ASEAN Summit news, photos, videos, and insights. For more updates and to share your own views, you can also join the Security and Global Affairs chat room in Rappler’s Muni app. Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva arrived in Manila on Friday, November 13, for a state visit ahead of his participation in the 49th Association of Southeast Asian Nations Summit. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Must Read Get to know the 11 ASEAN member states Close Pick up right where you left off. Switch to the Rappler app for a smoother, faster reading experience. Upgrade to Rappler+ for exclusive content and unlimited access",
