   "title": "Presidency Releases Mosque Footage To Counter Opposition Claims About Tinubu",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/presidency-releases-mosque-footage-to-counter-opposition-claims-about-tinubu/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:53:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794610380.0,
   "ageDays": 1.43,
   "summary": "The Presidency has released video footage showing President Bola Tinubu leaving a mosque after observing Friday prayers, in a move to counter claims circulating among opposition supporters about his whereabouts. He maintained that the footage released by the Presidency showed Tinubu leaving the mosque after observing the Friday congregational prayers.",
   "summary_zh": "总统府发布了一段视频画面，显示总统博拉·蒂努布在参加星期五主麻礼拜后离开清真寺，此举是为了反驳反对派支持者中流传的关于其行踪的说法。他坚持称，总统府发布的画面显示，蒂努布在参加星期五聚礼后离开了清真寺。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Presidency has released video footage showing President Bola Tinubu leaving a mosque after observing Friday prayers, in a move to counter claims circulating among opposition supporters about his whereabouts. Senior Adviser to the President on Digital and New Media, Otega Ogra shared the footage on his X handle on Friday, describing reports and videos being circulated by opposition supporters as misleading. In the post, Ogra accused the opposition of pushing a false narrative about the President, alleging that videos circulating online featured individuals he described as paid thugs at the mosque. He maintained that the footage released by the Presidency showed Tinubu leaving the mosque after observing the Friday congregational prayers. He added, “Contrary to the narrative being pushed by the opposition, with videos of their alleged paid thugs at the Mosque today, here is footage of Mr. President leaving the mosque after Friday prayers this afternoon.” The presidential aide accompanied the post with a message of support for Tinubu and the country, saying, “God bless our President. God bless Nigeria.” We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
